            <ArticleTitle>Asymptomatic bilateral hypernephroma: an autopsy case report wtih discussion of possible etiologic factors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>124-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first case of asymptomatic bilateral synchronous hypernephroma is described in a 52-year-old man who had a long history of alcoholic cirrhosis and died of uncontrollable gastrointestinal bleeding. The literature is reviewed briefly and relevant etiologic factors are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
